.TH "PB-CONFIG-LOCAL-ACCESS-PROXY" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-local-access-proxy - Route machine app names through Coolify or another reverse proxy


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config local-access proxy [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Otherwise-unmapped app names automatically use authorized port 80. Configure a different reverse-proxy port for a machine. Numeric port URLs and explicit aliases keep their destinations. This local setting never grants access; the proxy port must already be authorized.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for proxy


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config-local-access(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-local-access-proxy-set(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-local-access-proxy-unset(1)\fP
